# Optional. Copy to ~/.config/agent-status-tui/keepalive.env if the service
# needs environment systemd --user doesn't give it by default (it does not
# source your shell's rc files, so nvm/pyenv/etc. PATH additions from there
# are invisible to it). install.sh already resolves absolute paths to
# claude/codex/grok at install time, so this is only needed for anything
# those CLIs themselves shell out to and can't find.
#
# Never put secrets/tokens here or anywhere else in this setup: keepalive
# only ever runs a fixed "Reply only: OK" prompt and reads nothing but the
# process exit code, so it never needs, reads, or stores provider credentials.
#
# Example:
# PATH=/home/you/.nvm/versions/node/v20.11.0/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
